  31: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  32:     """Expand the sparse dot lattice into a 26x26 drawing with thick bars between adjacent matching dots.
  33: 
  34:     Input structure
  35:     - The background is the dominant color.
  36:     - Foreground pixels lie on logical rows and columns separated by background spacer rows/columns.
  37:     - A logical row or column is present when it contains at least one foreground pixel.
  38: 
  39:     Rule
  40:     - Expand every background spacer row/column to thickness 2.
  41:     - Expand the logical rows/columns equally so the full output is 26x26.
  42:     - Paint each foreground logical pixel as a solid rectangle of its color.
  43:     - Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels horizontally through the intervening spacer.
  44:     - Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels vertically only when neither endpoint is part of a horizontal same-color run.
  45: 
  46:     Key insight
  47:     - The input is a sampled line drawing: horizontal same-color runs define the bars first, and only unclaimed same-color vertical neighbors are joined.
  48:     """
